# What never enters the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named paths rather than `.`, so nothing here is
# strictly required today. It is here because the build context is sent to
# the daemon in full regardless of what the Dockerfile then copies, and
# because the next COPY someone adds is the one that picks up a local .env.
#
# The files that would carry credentials come first; the rest is size.

# Local configuration and credentials.
.env
*.env
!deploy/*.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# The database volume created by start_app.sh. Owner-only on the host, and
# not something to hand to the daemon or bake into a layer.
postgres_data/

# History, which includes every version of every file ever committed --
# including anything committed by mistake and removed later.
.git/
.gitignore

# Security-hardening tooling artifacts.
.sde-security/
.sde-handoff.json
.sde-apply-handoff.json
skills/

# Build and test residue.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
